        "canSeeDetail": true,
        "content": "### Approach: Simulation\n\n#### Intuition\n\nAccording to the definition, the reverse degree is computed as follows:\n\n- For each character $c$, multiply its position in the reversed alphabet by its 1-indexed position in the string.\n- Add all of these products.\n\nTraverse the string once. The reversed-alphabet position of a lowercase letter $c$ is $26 - (c - \\text{'a'})$. Multiplying this value by the character's 1-indexed position in the string and adding it to the running total produces the answer.\n\n#### Implementation\n\n<iframe src=\"https://leetcode.com/playground/WM3f48Vs/shared\" frameBorder=\"0\" width=\"100%\" height=\"225\" name=\"WM3f48Vs\"></iframe>\n\n#### Complexity Analysis\n\nLet $n$ be the length of the string.\n\n- Time complexity: $O(n)$.\n\n  We traverse the string once.\n\n- Space complexity: $O(1)$.\n\n---"
    },
